@host = http://localhost:5099
@customer = ada@example.test
@start = 2030-01-14T12:00:00
# Replace this with id returned by POST /bookings before running cancellation.
@bookingId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Quote. Monday Jan 14; deadline is Friday Jan 11, 2030, at 16:00 local business time.
GET {{host}}/quote?start={{start}}&hours=2&customerEmail={{customer}}

### Create (copy response id into bookingId above)
POST {{host}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "ada@example.test",
  "start": "2030-01-14T12:00:00",
  "hours": 2
}

### Inspect state
GET {{host}}/bookings

### Get one booking
GET {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### Cancel once; a repeated request is rejected without a second refund.
POST {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### Invalid time: expect 400
GET {{host}}/quote?start=2030-01-14T12:37:00&hours=1&customerEmail={{customer}}

